VMware paravirtual SCSI (PVSCSI) miniport, PCI 15AD:07C0 (also emulated by QEMU: -device pvscsi)

The driver (pvscsi.c) is new code, GPL-2.0-or-later, written against the legacy SCSI port
interface (scsiport) like the BusLogic miniport.

Origin of the device interface
  Project:  OpenBSD
  File:     sys/dev/pci/vmwpvs.c, revision 1.31 (2025/08/12)
  URL:      https://github.com/openbsd/src/blob/master/sys/dev/pci/vmwpvs.c
  License:  ISC, notice kept in the header of pvscsi.c
  Used:     the register offsets, the command numbers, the layouts of the request ring entry, the
            completion ring entry, the scatter/gather entry, the shared ring state and the
            SETUP_RINGS command. No code was copied: the OpenBSD driver is written for its own
            SCSI midlayer and DMA API.

Not used: the Linux driver vmw_pvscsi (GPL-2.0-only, not compatible with this tree), and any VMware
or Microsoft binary driver.

What it does not do: message ring (no hot plug of disks), MSI/MSI-X (INTx only), more than one
logical unit per target, CDBs longer than 16 bytes. Every index and context value that the device
writes (ring producer index, completion context) is range checked before it is used.
